                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_107">Cambridge, Cambridgeshire. St
                        John's College. </orgName><p>‘At Exod. xxv the name Kyngston in pencilled on
                        the lower margin. This is no doubt the John Kingston who owned no. 2 [i.e.
                        A.2, q.v.]’ (James, St John’s, 1)</p><p>‘At the end of Proverbs is a note
                        [...]: 1. I pointed (and revised) this book for my brother R. Levi on Friday
                        of the Pericope Tese’ (July-August) of the year 20 of the sixth thousand
                        (5020). May God make him worthy to study it, that it may not depart from his
                        mouth and from the mouth of his seed henceforth and for ever. 2. I, Samuel
                        Ha-naqdan (the Punctuator). This is followed by a short Hebrew rhyme. The
                        date is thus July-August A.D. 1260.’ (James, St John’s, 2)</p></provenance>
